ock", "targetName": "Art Rock", "context": "Genesis collaborated with visual artists and used elaborate stage setups, embodying the art rock ethos of blending music with visual art."}], "places": [{"name": "London, United Kingdom", "role": "Cultural Hub"}, {"name": "New York City, USA", "role": "Major Influence"}, {"name": "Berlin, Germany", "role": "Artistic Experimentation"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: art rock", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "art-rock"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q217467", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Art_rock"], "tags": ["music genre", "Music & Compositions", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "art rock contributed to the historical record of the Contemporary period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Art rock redefined the expectations of rock music during the late 20th century, influencing artists, genres, and cultural movements, and contributing to the evolution of thematic and conceptual approaches in music.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-25T01:05:13Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30137664636", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Art rock is a subgenre of rock music that aims to separate the genre from popular entertainment, with the term typically being applied as the middle ground between mainstream and experimental rock. Art rock primarily draws influences from the wider art world and academia; which includes contemporary art, art music, avant-garde art, experimental music, avant-garde music, alongside classical music and jazz.", "newValue": "Art rock emerged in the late 1960s, primarily in the United Kingdom, as a transformative subgenre of rock music that sought to elevate the genre beyond mere entertainment to an expressive art form. This movement was marked by notable bands such as Pink Floyd, Yes, and Genesis, who incorporated elements from classical music, avant-garde, and conceptual art into their compositions. The significance of art rock lies in its challenge to traditional rock norms and its aspiration to create a more profound, cerebral listening experience, reflecting broader cultural shifts toward intellectualism in music during the 1960s and 1970s.

The genre flourished during the early 1970s, with landmark albums like Pink Floyd's "The Dark Side of the Moon" (1973) and Genesis's "The Lamb Lies Down on Broadway" (1974) pushing the boundaries of what rock music could convey. These works often featured elaborate concept albums, thematic coherence, and innovative production techniques, which contributed to the genre’s distinct identity. Art rock artists frequently performed in elaborate stage shows that combined visual art and music, further blurring the lines between different artistic disciplines and attracting a diverse audience.

The legacy of art rock is profound, influencing not only future music genres such as progressive rock and post-rock but also impacting visual arts and performance art. Artists and bands that followed, including Radiohead and Björk, have cited art rock as a significant influence on their work, demonstrating its lasting impact on the evolution of popular music. The genre also paved the way for the acceptance of experimental sounds in mainstream music, leading to a broader appreciation for artistic expression within the rock genre."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-25T01:05:13Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30137664636", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Cultural, artistic, or intellectual creation"], "newValue": ["The rise of counterculture movements in the 1960s encouraged experimentation in music and art.", "The influence of European avant-garde music and visual art challenged musicians to explore new forms of expression.", "Technological advancements in music production allowed for more complex arrangements and soundscapes."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-25T01:05:13Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30137664636", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission"], "newValue": ["Art rock expanded the boundaries of rock music, allowing for greater artistic expression and complexity.", "The genre influenced subsequent musical movements, including progressive rock and alternative music, shaping the landscape of modern music.", "Art rock's emphasis on concept albums and thematic coherence paved the way for the narrative-driven music of the late 20th century."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-25T01:05:13Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30137664636", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "art-rock", "sourceName": "art rock", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "era-contemporary", "targetName": "Contemporary", "context": "art rock is situated within the Contemporary (960)"}], "new